195 0 obj
  << /ActualText (RupeeRise\nDesigning for safe financial behaviour\054 not just financial knowledge\nTimeline\072 14\055day hackathon \050parallel to full\055time role\051\050Role\072 Lead Product Designer \050UX\054 UI\054 Product Thinking\051\050Platform\072 Mobile\055first application\n1\056 Context\nThe hackathon brief focused on improving financial literacy among teenagers and young earners\056\nThe initial assumption was that users lacked financial knowledge\054 and that better tracking and education could solve the problem\056\nHowever\054 during exploration\054 it became clear that exposure to financial tools had increased significantly\056 Many users already had access to investing apps and financial content\056\nThe challenge was not access\056\050 It was behaviour\056\n2\056 Refined Problem\nYoung earners\072\nAre exposed to investing early\nAre influenced by short\055term gain narratives\nOften feel anxious or overconfident\nLack structured progression before risking real money\nThe real gap was not information\056\nIt was the absence of behavioural guardrails\056\nRupeeRise therefore focused on\072\nHelping users develop stable financial behaviour before increasing exposure to risk\056\nFinancial literacy remained important \024 but as a supporting layer\054 not the end goal\056\n3\056 Constraints\n14\055day timeline\nResearch conducted during weekday evenings\nDesign and prototyping over weekends\nLightweight but focused validation\nGiven the time constraint\054 the goal was not scale validation\054 but clarity of direction and responsible system design\056\n4\056 Research Snapshot\nPrimary Inputs\nInformal interviews with early earners and young professionals\nDiscussions around spending anxiety\054 credit usage\054 and investing hesitation\nSecondary Inputs\nReview of Indian fintech and investing platforms\nAnalysis of finfluencer content and beginner investing journeys\nKey Observations\nUsers fear irreversible financial loss\056\nFinancial dashboards often increase anxiety instead of clarity\056\nBeginners either avoid investing completely or jump in impulsively\056\nConsistency matters more than feature depth\056\nThese observations shaped the behavioural focus of the product\056\n5\056 Core Metric\nThe core metric for RupeeRise is\072\nBehavioural progression toward stable financial decision\055making\056\nThis includes\072\nConsistent tracking habits\nCompletion of learning modules\nSimulation engagement before real exposure\nGradual\054 controlled increase in investment limits\nSuccess is defined by behavioural maturity\054 not transaction volume\056\n6\056 Product Structure \024 Four Supporting Pillars\nThe system was designed around four connected pillars\056\n1\017\343 Behaviour Awareness\nTracking is included not as a generic feature\054 but as a behavioural signal layer\056\nIt\072\nIdentifies discretionary spending patterns\nSupports budget awareness\nEnables context\055based nudges\nPurpose\072\050 Ensure investment decisions are grounded in real financial capacity\056\n2\017\343 Structured Learning\nLearning modules simplify key financial concepts and validate understanding through short quizzes\056\nLearning acts as\072\nConfidence building\nProgress gating\nPreparation for exposure\nPurpose\072\050 Knowledge as readiness\054 not as isolated content\056\n3\017\343 Simulation Before Capital\nAll users begin with simulation using real market data\056\nWhy\072\nExperience volatility safely\nUnderstand price movement emotionally\nReduce fear before committing capital\nSimulation is mandatory in early stages and adaptive in mature stages\056\nPurpose\072\050 Practice before risk\056\n4\017\343 Adaptive Guardrails\nThe system adjusts friction based on behavioural maturity\072\nGuarded Mode \050higher friction\054 strict caps\051\nGuided Mode \050moderate friction\051\nAutonomous Mode \050lower friction\054 critical alerts remain active\051\nIf risky patterns re\055emerge\054 friction is gradually reintroduced\056\nPurpose\072\050 Encourage independence without removing safety\056\n7\056 Interaction Philosophy\nPrimary tone\072 Calming\050 Secondary\072 Stabilising\050 Tertiary\072 Light gamification\nDesign choices reflect this\072\nProgress\055first home screen\nClear hierarchy\nLimited colour emphasis\nNo urgency\055based notifications\nThe product intentionally avoids stimulation\055driven engagement\056\n8\056 Monetization Consideration \050Long\055Term\051\nIf scaled\054 monetization would align with behavioural safety\072\nMentor sessions\nAdvanced analytics\nGoal\055aligned financial partnerships\nHigh\055risk asset promotion or impulse\055driven advertising would contradict the system\031s philosophy and are intentionally excluded\056\n9\056 Validation \046 Feedback\nDuring the hackathon\072\nUsers responded positively to the simulation\055first approach\056\nProgress framing felt less stressful than balance\055heavy dashboards\056\nJury feedback acknowledged the responsible structure and system\055level thinking\054 while noting the need for long\055term validation to measure sustained behavioural change\056\nGiven the time constraint\054 long\055term behavioural measurement was outside scope\056\n10\056 Reflection\nRupeeRise began as a financial literacy concept\056\nIt evolved into a behaviour\055first financial system\056\nThe key learning was that\072\nDesigning for financial behaviour requires balancing autonomy and guardrails\056\050 Reducing risk is not about restricting users permanently\054 but about guiding them toward stable independence\056)
